  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.542) and config_003 showed avgpool > transformer for the same encoder pair, establishing avgpool+weighted as the preferred aggregation/fusion. The biggest remaining uncertainty is whether the large imagenet_vit_l image encoder is actually contributing meaningfully or whether a lighter resnet50 backbone could perform comparably (or even better due to less overfitting). This experiment (config_039) is a clean single-variable test: it swaps only the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l to resnet50 while holding scgpt, avgpool, weighted, and multiprofile fixed. If resnet50 matches or exceeds 0.542, we gain a cheaper backbone for all subsequent experiments, freeing GPU budget. If it drops significantly, we confirm ViT-L is essential and can focus remaining budget on RNA-encoder and fusion variations. Expected cost: ~2.3–2.6 GPU hours, modestly cheaper than config_001 (2.94) since ResNet-50 has fewer parameters than ViT-Large."
}

